      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking again, this still consumes global VNET buffer bit 27: removing AVAIL9 also removes it from VNET_BUFFER_FLAGS_ALL_AVAIL. The foundation does not name the owner or document the flag\u0027s set/clear lifetime, so the reservation is implicit. Could we avoid the flag entirely, or at least define and document an IPTFS-owned flag explicitly?",
      "parentUuid": "73d92e00_33b41580",
      "revId": "91527b5f1d8a06899a6c27c8b340b645ac490202",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b88adcf_75e4c76d",
        "filename": "src/vnet/ipsec/esp_decrypt.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T09:36:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we avoid restoring these values into vnet_buffer(b)-\u003eipsec? esp_post_data(b)-\u003edecrypt_data already persists in the buffer\u0027s unused opaque area for the async handoff and contains sa_index, seq, and seq_hi. IPTFS can consume that record directly. The sync path may need to save its stack-local pd into the same record before handoff, but that avoids both repurposing IPsec opaque metadata and the extra async copy.",
      "parentUuid": "bae228d4_ef8ff11a",
      "revId": "91527b5f1d8a06899a6c27c8b340b645ac490202",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "03860466_d380044d",
        "filename": "src/vnet/ipsec/ipsec.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T09:36:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This introduces IPTFS-specific callbacks, configuration parsing, formatting, SA/policy lifecycle, tunnel feature handling, and output-node state into generic IPsec. Could the implementation instead live in an IPTFS-owned subtree, with core IPsec exposing only narrow generic integration points such as next-header registration and, if required, a generic SA output-next override? That would keep the substantial IPTFS implementation isolated and replace the distributed tfs_* callback contract with direct, type-checked ownership.",
      "revId": "91527b5f1d8a06899a6c27c8b340b645ac490202",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b4d170f_0feed702",
        "filename": "src/vnet/ipsec/ipsec_api.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T09:36:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another serialization issue remains in this new dump API: ipsec_sad_tfs_type_decode() converts its input from network byte order, but ipsec_sad_tfs_type_encode() returns host-order enum values. On little-endian systems ipsec_sa_v6_dump therefore exposes an invalid TFS type to clients. Could the encoder return clib_host_to_net_u32() of the selected value?",
      "parentUuid": "9e40df55_546cbb16",
      "revId": "91527b5f1d8a06899a6c27c8b340b645ac490202",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89a06d14_2dc3ba20",
        "filename": "src/vnet/ipsec/ipsec_api.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1510,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T09:36:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unlike the v5 dump, the new v6 dump populates replay_window but not entry.anti_replay_window_size. A non-default anti-replay window cannot be reconstructed from v6 dump output. Could this mirror the v5 assignment from irt-\u003eanti_replay_window_size?",
      "revId": "91527b5f1d8a06899a6c27c8b340b645ac490202",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "569d1895_221420a0",
        "filename": "src/vnet/ipsec/ipsec_sa.c",
